  "title": "Shi et al. 2025 — HEFMI-ICH: a hybrid EEG-fNIRS motor imagery dataset for brain-computer interface in intracerebral hemorrhage",
  "description": "HEFMI-ICH is a hybrid EEG-fNIRS motor imagery dataset for brain-computer interface research in intracerebral hemorrhage. This BIDS release contains 32-channel EEG from 37 participants (17 healthy controls and 20 ICH patients) performing left- and right-hand motor imagery across 98 sessions. It is intended for BCI-based rehabilitation research and benchmarking of motor imagery decoding methods.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 256 Hz from 32 channels with a g.HIamp amplifier (g.tec). Participants performed a two-class (left/right hand grasping) motor imagery task, cued by a directional arrow and an auditory beep. Each session comprised 30 trials (15 per class), with a 10 s imagery period. Sessions were consecutive runs recorded on the same day.",
